`dart format --set-exit-if-changed` on SDK 3.13.5 (the current stable, i.e. what CI's `setup-dart@stable` resolves to) re-wraps two `test(...)` call sites in this file — e.g. this one becomes the tall-style:

```dart
test(
  'values below 1 clamp UP to 1.0 — the scale never shrinks a budget',
  () {
    ...
  },
);
```

The PR description claims "`dart format`: clean", so this was likely formatted with a different SDK/build of the formatter. CI does not gate on `dart format` (the pre-commit hook self-heals, but hook-only), so it won't red a leg — just run `dart format test/cli/pty_wait_budget_test.dart` at next touch to keep the tree convergent with the hook.
